# Evidence (runtime artifacts — large, generated)
evidence/
!evidence/.gitkeep

# P065 Step 1: committed, sanitized real-Codex capture sample — this is a small,
# fixed, deliberately-tracked grounding artifact (not a runtime evidence dump),
# but the generic `evidence/` rule above blindly matches any dir named
# `evidence` anywhere in the tree, including this one. Re-include ONLY this
# specific committed sample, not the whole `e2e/evidence/` tree (CP2 finding:
# a broader negation here reproduces the same "catches too much" problem one
# level down — a future unsanitized runtime dump elsewhere under e2e/evidence/
# would be silently re-included too).
#
# P065 Step 13 fix: the two negations directly below (added in Step 1) look
# like they re-include codex-stream-sample/, but on their own they DON'T —
# git's own documented rule is "a negated pattern cannot re-include a path
# whose PARENT directory is still excluded", and the bare `evidence/` rule
# above excludes this whole directory (incl. traversal) before any deeper
# negation is even considered. `git add` on a brand-new file dropped into
# codex-stream-sample/ was verified to be REFUSED as ignored — the two
# files already there only stayed tracked because they were added before/
# via -f, not because the negation worked. Fixed by un-ignoring this exact
# `evidence/` directory FIRST (so git descends into it again), then
# re-excluding its bare contents with `evidence/*`, then re-including only
# the specific reviewed artifacts below — never the whole tree (a future
# unsanitized runtime dump elsewhere under e2e/evidence/ must stay ignored).
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/
plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/*
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/codex-stream-sample/
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/codex-stream-sample/**

# P065 Step 13: committed, sanitized real-Codex dogfood proof (attestation + a
# re-hashed regression fixture). Same "narrow negation, not the whole tree"
# rule as codex-stream-sample above — do NOT widen this to
# `!.../e2e/evidence/` or `!.../e2e/evidence/**`; that would silently
# re-include any FUTURE unsanitized runtime dump under e2e/evidence/ too.
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-live-attestation.md
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture/
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture/**

# IMP-245 follow-up: real-AC dogfood proof (pass + fail cases) — same narrow
# negation rule, same reasoning.
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture-real-ac-pass-live-attestation.md
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture-real-ac-pass/
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture-real-ac-pass/**
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture-real-ac-fail-live-attestation.md
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture-real-ac-fail/
!plugins/aid-orchestrator/scripts/tests/e2e/evidence/c3-dogfood-fixture-real-ac-fail/**

# Development workspace (session logs, active work, internal docs)
workspace/

# Reference specs (internal, not for distribution)
_unzipped/

# Internal documentation, design notes, plans, audits, and project-local docs.
# Public GitHub should contain plugin/runtime assets and plugin-facing docs in
# plugin paths, not private planning material under docs/.
docs/
# EXCEPTION: the live-probe findings ledger must stay tracked — it was
# accidentally caught by a merge-conflict "delete" resolution on 2026-07-08
# specifically because it lost tracking here with no negation rule. Restored
# 2026-07-09; do not remove this line without an explicit decision to stop
# tracking findings history.
!docs/plans/BACKLOG.md

# AID workspace (created by /aid-init for dogfooding — not for distribution)
.aid-o/
# Test suites call aid-fsm.sh init and create nested .aid-o/ workspaces
**/.aid-o/

# Claude Code local settings + per-project memory file
# (CLAUDE.md is the project's private context for Claude Code — contains
# internal infra refs, ops paths, personal context that shouldn't be on a
# public repo. The .MD upper-case entry that lived here previously did not
# match CLAUDE.md on case-sensitive filesystems, so the file was tracked
# despite the gitignore intent. This pair (lower + upper) covers both.)
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.MD

